## A S S I G N M E N T O V E R V I E W

SQL Aggregation Functions, GROUP BY & HAVING:
This assignment focuses on SQL aggregation functions and how they are
used with
GROUP BY and HAVING to analyze and summarize data.
Instead of displaying individual rows, you will learn how to write queries
that produce meaningful summaries, such as totals, averages, counts, and
comparisons across different categories.

By completing this assignment, you will be able to:
Use aggregation functions such as
COUNT(), SUM(), AVG(), MAX(), and MIN()
Group data correctly using GROUP BY
Filter aggregated results using HAVING
Understand the difference between WHERE and HAVING
Write correct and well-structured analytical SQL queries

Load the provided dataset into your database
Read each question carefully
Identify whether GROUP BY and/or HAVING is required
Focus on understanding the logic behind each query
